// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #6451 Add macOS encoded payload piped to shell rule
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6451
// Pull request author: yana-ivanov
// Change: new rule
// Title: Suspicious Encoded Payload Piped To Shell - macOS
// Sigma ID: b9a60caf-969e-4033-9513-2f097adee039
// Status: experimental | Level: high
// Author: Yana Ivanov
// Date: 2026-10-10 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, command-and-control, T1059.004, T1105, T1027
// Description: Detects a command line that downloads content with curl, decodes it with base64 or gunzip, and
//   pipes the result into a shell interpreter. This chain is used by macOS ClickFix campaigns, where
//   a user is socially engineered into pasting a prepared command into Terminal, and by the MacSync
//   and AMOS infostealer infection chains. The decode step is what separates this from legitimate
//   installer one-liners, which fetch and execute without decoding.
// False positives:
//   - Installation scripts that fetch a compressed archive and pipe it through a shell, which is uncommon but not unheard of in developer tooling
// References:
//   - https://www.microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/08/18/hunting-macsync-stealer-infrastructure-through-behavioral-pivots/
//   - https://securelist.com/macsync-new-version/121383/
//   - https://hunt.io/blog/macos-clickfix-applescript-terminal-phishing
//   - https://unit42.paloaltonetworks.com/atomic-macos-amos-stealer-activity
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/746407b8668625051554d31bf2574686b1a62b55/rules/macos/process_creation/proc_creation_macos_susp_encoded_payload_piped_to_shell.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where ProcessCommandLine contains "curl" and (ProcessCommandLine contains "base64 -d" or ProcessCommandLine contains "base64 --decode" or ProcessCommandLine contains "gunzip" or ProcessCommandLine contains "gzip -d" or ProcessCommandLine contains "xxd -r") and (ProcessCommandLine contains "| sh" or ProcessCommandLine contains "|sh" or ProcessCommandLine contains "| bash" or ProcessCommandLine contains "|bash" or ProcessCommandLine contains "| zsh" or ProcessCommandLine contains "|zsh" or ProcessCommandLine contains "| /bin/sh" or ProcessCommandLine contains "| /bin/bash" or ProcessCommandLine contains "| /bin/zsh" or ProcessCommandLine contains "|/bin/sh" or ProcessCommandLine contains "|/bin/bash" or ProcessCommandLine contains "|/bin/zsh")
